# them, so that one which moved fails `make check-zip-corpus`
# rather than quietly becoming the new expectation.
# Regenerated by `make zip-corpus`.
#
# A digest of `-` is a fixture whose bytes are not a function
# of its inputs - a random salt, a random encryption header, an
# unsettable ctime. It stays in the list so that its absence is
# still a failure, and manifest.tsv, which is hashed, is what
# covers what is inside it. See NOT_REPRODUCIBLE in
# tools/oracle/make_zip_corpus.py for which and why.
